    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0229" n="127" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/508: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-17T15:00:00+00:00">October 17, 1935—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 17—9:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>522. By appointment Atherton and Anderson called at the Foreign Office today and
                    set forth the points of Department’s 300, October 14, 6 p.m., which the British
                    received with evident satisfaction. A précis of conversation was left, based on
                    the Department’s instruction (copies by pouch tomorrow<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d129-f1"/>) and the British will seek another meeting shortly, after
                    they have studied it, and formulated a précis of conversation for reply.</p>
                <p>It was agreed that these précis of conversation would not constitute an “exchange
                    of written official papers or memoranda”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
